Package: lsogscore
Title: Late-Successional and Old-Growth Scoring Instruments for Maine and New Brunswick
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aaron", "Weiskittel", email = "aaron.weiskittel@maine.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Christopher W.", "Woodall", role = "aut"),
    person("Anthony W.", "D'Amato", role = "aut"))
Description: One tested implementation of every late-successional and old-growth
    (LSOG) scoring instrument used in the Maine and New Brunswick analysis, in
    place of the seven scattered R and Python implementations that preceded it.
    Covers the Maine published six-axis card, the New Brunswick published
    five-axis card, the strict four-axis conjunctive rule, the CORE4 comparable
    instrument, both CORE5 forms, and the two small-area-estimation label cards.
    Every threshold is stored in the units its source code used, carries the file
    and line it came from, and is converted once at a single boundary, so a
    jurisdiction difference is visible rather than silently harmonized. No plot
    coordinate is read, written, or required.
